The world’s largest restaurant chain now has a presence in the United States. Mixue, a concept that features ice cream, teas, and coffee, opened on Hollywood Boulevard in Los Angeles Dec. 19, adding to its global footprint that includes more than 53,000 stores worldwide.&nbsp;

By comparison, Starbucks has about 40,000 stores in 88 markets, while Subway has about 37,000 locations, and KFC has just over 30,000.

